<title>HONG KONG: China Light up after power venture deal.</title>
<headline>China Light up after power venture deal.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of China Light and Power Co Ltd rose on overseas buying after it announced the signing a Shenzhen power plant joint venture agreement with a unit of Exxon Corp, brokers said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;The deal is seen to be positive in the longer run and it gives investors an excuse to buy, but we did not see the deal to have any immediate contribution to the company earnings,&quot; said Sean Li, associate director at Amsteel Securities.</p>
<p>China Light shares rose HK$0.70 or 2.03 percent to HK$35.20 in mid-morning on volume of 4.18 million shares.</p>
</text>
